        "method": "<javax.validation.ConstraintValidatorContext: javax.validation.ConstraintValidatorContext$ConstraintViolationBuilder buildConstraintViolationWithTemplate(java.lang.String)>",
        "index": 0
      },
      "why": "The String passed as argument 0 is used to build a constraint violation message template. In Bean Validation, message templates support interpolation using Expression Language (EL). If an attacker can control the cron expression or any part of the error message context that gets interpolated into this template string, it could lead to EL injection (CWE-094). Although this specific call site uses a hardcoded string, the method signature itself is a sink for EL injection vulnerabilities if the argument were user-controlled.",
